# Every text file of the plugin is checked out with LF line endings on every
# platform. Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which would otherwise
# give the hook scripts CRLF endings: the shebang becomes `bash\r` and the hook
# never starts, and `set -o pipefail` fails under an explicit bash — so the
# guards would not run. Claude Code installs plugins with Git, so this also
# applies to developers' installed copies (0.9.1).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts run under bash on every platform, including Windows Git Bash.
*.sh text eol=lf
# Node helpers, the hook library's Node fallback, the preflight and the hook registration.
*.ts text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf

# Exceptions — below the general rules, so they win.
#
# Deliberate hazards: these migration fixtures must keep CRLF line endings and trailing
# whitespace byte-for-byte (see scripts/fixtures/planning-docs/README.md), so they are
# never converted, and git's whitespace checks do not apply to them.
scripts/fixtures/planning-docs/fa-hazards.md -text -whitespace
scripts/fixtures/planning-docs/fa-hazards.expected.md -text -whitespace
